{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"opposite number opposite number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","fileName":"Opposite Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Opposite Number","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Number Systems and Arithmetic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Number Line","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"opposite number opposite number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","fileName":"Opposite Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Opposite Number","heading":"Opposite Number","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The opposite of a number (a) is the number (-a) that combines with it to produce the additive identity:\n\n$$a+(-a)=0.$$\n\nOpposites lie the same distance from zero on opposite sides of the [[Number Line]]. Taking the opposite twice returns the original value, so (-(-a)=a). The notation does not say a number is negative by itself: if (a<0), then (-a>0). Subtraction can be defined as addition of an opposite, (a-b=a+(-b)).","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Number Line","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"opposite number opposite number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Opposite Number.md","fileName":"Opposite Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Opposite Number","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Number Line","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}